00:10:55,070 --> 00:10:57,029
nine hundred twenty dollars.

281
00:10:57,209 --> 00:10:59,098
And the Nissan Frontier,

282
00:10:59,098 --> 00:11:00,987
at thirty-six point six,

283
00:11:00,987 --> 00:11:03,269
would lose fourteen thousand,

284
00:11:03,269 --> 00:11:04,686
six hundred forty.

285
00:11:04,866 --> 00:11:07,443
So between the Tacoma and the Frontier,

286
00:11:07,443 --> 00:11:10,021
the same starting price would leave you

287
00:11:10,021 --> 00:11:12,268
with a difference of six thousand,

288
00:11:12,268 --> 00:11:14,846
eight hundred forty dollars in what the

289
00:11:14,846 --> 00:11:15,837
truck is worth.

290
00:11:16,187 --> 00:11:20,013
Second example, a heavy-duty truck that costs

291
00:11:20,013 --> 00:11:22,479
seventy thousand dollars new.

292
00:11:22,659 --> 00:11:25,304
The Ram three thousand five hundred,

293
00:11:25,304 --> 00:11:27,361
at twenty point two percent,

294
00:11:27,361 --> 00:11:29,491
would lose fourteen thousand,

295
00:11:29,491 --> 00:11:31,401
one hundred forty dollars.

296
00:11:31,581 --> 00:11:35,136
The Ford F-three-fifty would lose fourteen thousand,

297
00:11:35,136 --> 00:11:36,434
two hundred eighty.

298
00:11:36,614 --> 00:11:40,336
The F-four-fifty would lose sixteen thousand,

299
00:11:40,336 --> 00:11:41,328
one hundred.

300
00:11:41,508 --> 00:11:45,293
The F-two-fifty, seventeen thousand and ten.

301
00:11:45,473 --> 00:11:48,254
And the Ram two thousand five hundred,

302
00:11:48,254 --> 00:11:51,255
seventeen thousand, five hundred seventy.

303
00:11:51,605 --> 00:11:54,707
Third example, a small truck that costs

304
00:11:54,707 --> 00:11:56,934
thirty thousand dollars new.

305
00:11:57,114 --> 00:12:00,786
The Maverick, at thirty-one point eight percent,

306
00:12:00,786 --> 00:12:02,699
would lose nine thousand,

307
00:12:02,699 --> 00:12:04,765
five hundred forty dollars.

308
00:12:04,945 --> 00:12:06,058
The Santa Cruz,

309
00:12:06,058 --> 00:12:07,989
at thirty-four point nine,

310
00:12:07,989 --> 00:12:09,771
would lose ten thousand,

311
00:12:09,771 --> 00:12:11,330
four hundred seventy.

312
00:12:11,510 --> 00:12:14,134
The difference is nine hundred thirty dollars.

313
00:12:14,314 --> 00:12:15,468
Not very large,

314
00:12:15,468 --> 00:12:17,854
but it is money that comes back

315
00:12:17,854 --> 00:12:19,393
to you, or does not,

316
00:12:19,393 --> 00:12:20,932
on the day you sell.

317
00:12:21,282 --> 00:12:24,635
Fourth example, the one that matters most,

318
00:12:24,635 --> 00:12:28,067
a full-size truck that costs sixty thousand

319
00:12:28,067 --> 00:12:29,025
dollars new.

320
00:12:29,205 --> 00:12:32,459
The Tundra, at nineteen point seven percent,

321
00:12:32,459 --> 00:12:34,456
would lose eleven thousand,

322
00:12:34,456 --> 00:12:36,601
eight hundred twenty dollars.

323
00:12:36,781 --> 00:12:39,498
The Ram one thousand five hundred would

324
00:12:39,498 --> 00:12:41,239
lose twenty-two thousand,

325
00:12:41,239 --> 00:12:42,632
nine hundred twenty.

326
00:12:42,812 --> 00:12:46,548
The F-one-fifty would lose twenty-three thousand,

327
00:12:46,548 --> 00:12:47,921
one hundred sixty.

328
00:12:48,101 --> 00:12:50,882
And the Sierra one thousand five hundred

329
00:12:50,882 --> 00:12:53,176
would lose twenty-three thousand,

330
00:12:53,176 --> 00:12:54,150
seven hundred.

331
00:12:54,500 --> 00:12:56,640
Look at the gap in that last

332
00:12:56,640 --> 00:12:57,251
example.

333
00:12:57,431 --> 00:12:59,753
Between the Tundra and the Ram,

334
00:12:59,753 --> 00:13:02,899
the difference in loss is eleven thousand,

335
00:13:02,899 --> 00:13:04,397
one hundred dollars.

336
00:13:04,577 --> 00:13:06,995
Between the Tundra and the Sierra,

337
00:13:06,995 --> 00:13:09,697
eleven thousand, eight hundred eighty.

338
00:13:09,877 --> 00:13:11,705
That is a large number,

339
00:13:11,705 --> 00:13:13,772
and it is the same size as

340
00:13:13,772 --> 00:13:15,044
a good used car.

341
00:13:15,224 --> 00:13:17,087
It is the reason why a buyer

342
00:13:17,087 --> 00:13:19,017
who plans to keep a truck for

343
00:13:19,017 --> 00:13:21,812
only five years should think about resale,

344
00:13:21,812 --> 00:13:24,407
and not only about the monthly payment.

345
00:13:24,757 --> 00:13:26,626
Now the honest counterpoint.

346
00:13:26,806 --> 00:13:29,225
The Tundra and the Ram are different

347
00:13:29,225 --> 00:13:31,307
trucks, with different engines,

348
00:13:31,307 --> 00:13:34,062
different prices, and different features.

349
00:13:34,242 --> 00:13:36,913
A buyer who chooses the Ram because

350
00:13:36,913 --> 00:13:38,897
they prefer how it drives,

351
00:13:38,897 --> 00:13:40,652
or how much it can tow,

352
00:13:40,652 --> 00:13:43,017
or the price they were offered,

353
00:13:43,017 --> 00:13:45,306
is making a reasonable choice.

354
00:13:45,486 --> 00:13:48,737
Resale value is one number among many.

355
00:13:48,917 --> 00:13:50,198
It should be in your decision,

356
00:13:50,198 --> 00:13:51,435
but it should not be the only

357
00:13:51,435 --> 00:13:51,947
thing in it.

358
00:13:52,298 --> 00:13:54,027
So what is the lesson?

359
00:13:54,207 --> 00:13:57,365
Resale value is part of the price.

360
00:13:57,545 --> 00:14:00,138
A cheaper truck that loses more is

361
00:14:00,138 --> 00:14:02,120
not always cheaper to own.

362
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:04,870
And an expensive truck that keeps its

363
00:14:04,870 --> 00:14:07,300
value can cost less over five years

364
00:14:07,300 --> 00:14:09,315
than it looks like on the day

365
00:14:09,315 --> 00:14:10,148
of purchase.

366
00:14:10,328 --> 00:14:13,296
The heavy-duty trucks and the two Toyotas

367
00:14:13,296 --> 00:14:15,613
lose half as much as the typical

368
00:14:15,613 --> 00:14:17,713
half-ton, and that is a real,

369
00:14:17,713 --> 00:14:20,754
measurable difference in what you will pay

370
00:14:20,754 --> 00:14:21,984
to own the truck.

371
00:14:22,335 --> 00:14:24,168
But there is a counter-argument,

372
00:14:24,168 --> 00:14:25,028
and it is fair.

373
00:14:25,208 --> 00:14:27,887
A truck that holds its value usually

374
00:14:27,887 --> 00:14:29,226
costs more to buy,

375
00:14:29,226 --> 00:14:31,756
and buyers pay for the reputation.

376
00:14:31,936 --> 00:14:35,849
SlashGear notes that pickups hold value best

377
00:14:35,849 --> 00:14:37,983
of all vehicle segments,

378
00:14:37,983 --> 00:14:42,162
slightly ahead of fuel-sipping hybrids and well

379
00:14:42,162 --> 00:14:43,407
ahead of SUVs.

380
00:14:43,587 --> 00:14:46,239
So every truck on this list is,

381
00:14:46,239 --> 00:14:49,234
on average, a better store of value

382
00:14:49,234 --> 00:14:50,518
than most cars.

383
00:14:50,698 --> 00:14:52,823
The question is only how much better.

384
00:14:53,173 --> 00:14:54,322
One more warning.

385
00:14:54,502 --> 00:14:56,905
These are averages for the truck as

386
00:14:56,905 --> 00:14:58,278
it sold in the past,

387
00:14:58,278 --> 00:15:00,063
and the future can change.

388
00:15:00,243 --> 00:15:02,685
Prices of new trucks are rising,

389
00:15:02,685 --> 00:15:06,347
with the average full-size pickup at sixty-seven

390
00:15:06,347 --> 00:15:10,238
thousand, four hundred forty-six dollars in August,

391
00:15:10,238 --> 00:15:12,527
according to Kelley Blue Book.

392
00:15:12,707 --> 00:15:16,445
Electric trucks are being cancelled and rewritten.

393
00:15:16,625 --> 00:15:19,133
And a model that is discontinued can

394
00:15:19,133 --> 00:15:20,456
lose value quickly,

395
00:15:20,456 --> 00:15:21,153
or slowly.

396
00:15:21,333 --> 00:15:24,088
So treat these numbers as a guide,

397
00:15:24,088 --> 00:15:25,222
not a promise.

398
00:15:25,572 --> 00:15:28,370
Let's explain the key number in plain

399
00:15:28,370 --> 00:15:31,168
words, because it is easy to misread.

400
00:15:31,348 --> 00:15:33,840
When the Tacoma keeps eighty and a

401
00:15:33,840 --> 00:15:36,480
half percent of its value after five

402
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:39,266
years, it means that for every hundred

403
00:15:39,266 --> 00:15:40,512
dollars you paid,

404
00:15:40,512 --> 00:15:43,225
the truck is still worth about eighty

405
00:15:43,225 --> 00:15:46,011
dollars and fifty cents when you sell.

406
00:15:46,191 --> 00:15:50,362
When the F-one-fifty keeps sixty-one point four,

407
00:15:50,362 --> 00:15:53,751
it is worth about sixty-one dollars and

408
00:15:53,751 --> 00:15:54,794
forty cents.

409
00:15:54,974 --> 00:15:57,016
The rest is what you pay for

410
00:15:57,016 --> 00:15:58,256
owning the truck,

411
00:15:58,256 --> 00:16:00,590
and you pay it whether you drive

412
00:16:00,590 --> 00:16:02,486
ten miles or ten thousand.

413
00:16:02,836 --> 00:16:06,586
Now compare two figures we already saw.

414
00:16:06,766 --> 00:16:10,098
The Tundra keeps eighty and three tenths

415
00:16:10,098 --> 00:16:13,264
percent, and the Ram one thousand five

416
00:16:13,264 --> 00:16:16,263
hundred keeps sixty-one point eight.

417
00:16:16,443 --> 00:16:18,519
Both are full-size trucks,

418
00:16:18,519 --> 00:16:20,835
and both are sold at the same

419
00:16:20,835 --> 00:16:22,352
kind of dealership.

420
00:16:22,532 --> 00:16:24,887
But the gap between them is about

421
00:16:24,887 --> 00:16:27,742
eighteen points, and on a sixty thousand

422
00:16:27,742 --> 00:16:30,311
dollar truck it was eleven thousand,

423
00:16:30,311 --> 00:16:31,739
one hundred dollars.

424
00:16:31,919 --> 00:16:33,904
That is why we say the sticker

425
00:16:33,904 --> 00:16:35,228
is the first number.

426
00:16:35,408 --> 00:16:37,715
The second number can be larger than

427
00:16:37,715 --> 00:16:40,086
any discount you will ever negotiate.

428
00:16:40,437 --> 00:16:42,952
A very common buyer mistake is to

429
00:16:42,952 --> 00:16:45,696
look only at the monthly payment and

430
00:16:45,696 --> 00:16:46,915
ignore the exit.

431
00:16:47,095 --> 00:16:49,346
A payment tells you what the next

432
00:16:49,346 --> 00:16:50,369
few years cost.

433
00:16:50,549 --> 00:16:52,313
It does not tell you what you

434
00:16:52,313 --> 00:16:53,835
will get back at the end.

435
00:16:54,015 --> 00:16:55,103
Before you sign,

436
00:16:55,103 --> 00:16:56,871
ask yourself one question.

437
00:16:57,051 --> 00:16:59,321
If I sell this truck in five

438
00:16:59,321 --> 00:17:02,159
years, what do I expect to receive?

439
00:17:02,339 --> 00:17:04,727
Then look up the resale figure for

440
00:17:04,727 --> 00:17:05,922
that exact model,

441
00:17:05,922 --> 00:17:08,521
and write the expected amount next to

442
00:17:08,521 --> 00:17:10,698
the price you are paying today.

443
00:17:11,049 --> 00:17:13,184
The next question is how to verify

444
00:17:13,184 --> 00:17:14,566
what a truck is worth.

445
00:17:14,746 --> 00:17:16,709
Do not trust a single page.

446
00:17:16,889 --> 00:17:19,506
Look at the resale figure from the

447
00:17:19,506 --> 00:17:22,355
study, then check what the same model

448
00:17:22,355 --> 00:17:24,741
is listed for in your own area,

449
00:17:24,741 --> 00:17:27,744
with similar mileage and the same trim.

450
00:17:27,924 --> 00:17:30,107
Compare the same trim on the same

451
00:17:30,107 --> 00:17:32,158
day, so that the market has not

452
00:17:32,158 --> 00:17:34,077
moved between your two looks.

453
00:17:34,257 --> 00:17:36,224
And if a dealer quotes you a

454
00:17:36,224 --> 00:17:39,103
trade-in value, write it down and compare

455
00:17:39,103 --> 00:17:40,578
it to what you found,

456
00:17:40,578 --> 00:17:42,966
because the gap between the two is

457
00:17:42,966 --> 00:17:44,230
the dealer's room.

458
00:17:44,580 --> 00:17:46,553
There is also the paperwork.

459
00:17:46,733 --> 00:17:48,377
If you are buying used,

460
00:17:48,377 --> 00:17:50,379
ask for the service records,

461
00:17:50,379 --> 00:17:53,881
and run the vehicle identification number through

462
00:17:53,881 --> 00:17:54,953
a recall check,

463
00:17:54,953 --> 00:17:57,097
so you know that no safety fix

464
00:17:57,097 --> 00:17:59,528
is still open on that exact truck.

465
00:17:59,708 --> 00:18:02,195
If the truck has a remaining factory

466
00:18:02,195 --> 00:18:04,406
warranty, ask for it in writing,

467
00:18:04,406 --> 00:18:06,894
and ask whether it transfers to you.

468
00:18:07,074 --> 00:18:09,419
A truck with records and a clear

469
00:18:09,419 --> 00:18:11,763
history is easier to sell later,

470
00:18:11,763 --> 00:18:14,327
and that helps keep the very resale

471
00:18:14,327 --> 00:18:16,745
value we have been talking about.

472
00:18:17,095 --> 00:18:19,521
So who does this list suit?

473
00:18:19,701 --> 00:18:21,911
If you keep a truck for about

474
00:18:21,911 --> 00:18:23,815
five years and then sell,

475
00:18:23,815 --> 00:18:26,939
the Tacoma, the Tundra and the heavy-duty

476
00:18:26,939 --> 00:18:29,454
trucks are the ones that lose the

477
00:18:29,454 --> 00:18:32,120
least, and the Maverick is the best

478
00:18:32,120 --> 00:18:33,111
small choice.

479
00:18:33,291 --> 00:18:35,782
If you want a full-size half-ton from

480
00:18:35,782 --> 00:18:38,206
Detroit, you are buying a truck that

481
00:18:38,206 --> 00:18:40,159
loses close to forty percent,

482
00:18:40,159 --> 00:18:42,583
so the discount you negotiate on day

483
00:18:42,583 --> 00:18:43,728
one matters more.

484
00:18:43,908 --> 00:18:46,099
And if you will keep the truck

485
00:18:46,099 --> 00:18:48,509
for many years and drive it until

486
00:18:48,509 --> 00:18:51,357
it stops, resale matters much less than

487
00:18:51,357 --> 00:18:52,964
reliability and price.

488
00:18:53,314 --> 00:18:54,544
And who should wait?

489
00:18:54,724 --> 00:18:56,985
If you are looking at a truck

490
00:18:56,985 --> 00:18:58,933
that is being phased out,

491
00:18:58,933 --> 00:19:00,492
like the Santa Cruz,

492
00:19:00,492 --> 00:19:03,220
or a model whose future is unclear,

493
00:19:03,220 --> 00:19:04,233
do not guess.

494
00:19:04,413 --> 00:19:06,706
Ask whether it is still being built,

495
00:19:06,706 --> 00:19:08,935
and ask the dealer for the warranty

496
00:19:08,935 --> 00:19:10,973
and the service plan in writing.

497
00:19:11,153 --> 00:19:13,296
A good truck can keep a decent

498
00:19:13,296 --> 00:19:15,582
share of its value even after it

499
00:19:15,582 --> 00:19:19,082
is discontinued, but the reports are unconfirmed.

500
00:19:19,262 --> 00:19:21,455
When the future of a model is

501
00:19:21,455 --> 00:19:24,556
unclear, patience is cheaper than regret.

502
00:19:24,907 --> 00:19:27,423
One last way to use this video

503
00:19:27,423 --> 00:19:29,017
is as a tiebreaker.

504
00:19:29,197 --> 00:19:31,570
Say you have narrowed your choice to

505
00:19:31,570 --> 00:19:33,943
two trucks that cost about the same,

506
00:19:33,943 --> 00:19:35,129
and you like both.

507
00:19:35,309 --> 00:19:37,631
Look at the resale figure for each.

508
00:19:37,811 --> 00:19:39,936
If one keeps far more of its

509
00:19:39,936 --> 00:19:42,744
value, as the Tacoma does against the

510
00:19:42,744 --> 00:19:45,704
Frontier, then the second truck needs a

511
00:19:45,704 --> 00:19:47,146
real reason to win,

512
00:19:47,146 --> 00:19:49,422
such as a feature you will use

513
00:19:49,422 --> 00:19:50,257
every week.

514
00:19:50,437 --> 00:19:51,872
If the two are close,

515
00:19:51,872 --> 00:19:54,194
as the Maverick and the Santa Cruz

516
00:19:54,194 --> 00:19:56,448
are, then choose on how the truck

517
00:19:56,448 --> 00:19:58,703
drives, and on the price you were

518
00:19:58,703 --> 00:19:59,249
offered.

519
00:19:59,599 --> 00:20:01,512
So what should you check before you

520
00:20:01,512 --> 00:20:02,989
buy in twenty twenty-seven?

521
00:20:03,169 --> 00:20:06,527
First, look up the five-year resale value

522
00:20:06,527 --> 00:20:08,083
of the exact model,

523
00:20:08,083 --> 00:20:09,229
not the brand.

524
00:20:09,409 --> 00:20:12,299
Second, compare the full cost over five

525
00:20:12,299 --> 00:20:15,188
years, including what you expect to get

526
00:20:15,188 --> 00:20:16,596
back when you sell.

527
00:20:16,776 --> 00:20:20,390
Third, check the mileage and condition rules

528
00:20:20,390 --> 00:20:22,444
that affect resale value,

529
00:20:22,444 --> 00:20:25,401
because a truck with high mileage is

530
00:20:25,401 --> 00:20:27,701
worth less than the average.

531
00:20:27,881 --> 00:20:30,729
And fourth, ask whether the truck is

532
00:20:30,729 --> 00:20:32,153
still being built.

533
00:20:32,503 --> 00:20:34,335
We put all of this into a

534
00:20:34,335 --> 00:20:38,366
checklist, the Twenty Twenty-Seven Truck Buyer's Guide.

535
00:20:38,546 --> 00:20:40,605
It covers the numbers to check,

536
00:20:40,605 --> 00:20:42,599
the questions to ask a dealer,

537
00:20:42,599 --> 00:20:45,256
and the warning signs we walked through.

538
00:20:45,436 --> 00:20:47,769
The link is in the description and

539
00:20:47,769 --> 00:20:49,279
in the pinned comment.

540
00:20:49,459 --> 00:20:51,888
If you want to know which engines

541
00:20:51,888 --> 00:20:53,729
to avoid in a used truck,

542
00:20:53,729 --> 00:20:56,599
subscribe, because that is coming soon.

543
00:20:56,779 --> 00:20:57,940
Thanks for watching.
